    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "We often use these "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "gestures",
            "ref": "v-gesture"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". But do you know that each of them has an "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "origin",
            "ref": "v-origin"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "? Read on to find out more!"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "h1",
        "type": "heading",
        "level": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "V sign"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "The V sign played a "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "role",
            "zh": "发挥作用"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " in "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "World War II",
            "zh": "第二次世界大战"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". Many people used it to stand for “"
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "victory",
            "ref": "v-victory"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "”. So did Winston Churchill*! Later in the 1960s, this sign began to stand for “"
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "peace",
            "ref": "v-peace"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "” among young people in America and Britain."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "h2",
        "type": "heading",
        "level": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "Thumbs-up",
            "zh": "竖大拇指"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "In "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "ancient Rome",
            "zh": "古罗马"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", people watched "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "gladiatorial",
            "zh": "角斗士的"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "combats",
            "zh": "格斗"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". By using different gestures, they decided "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "whether",
            "zh": "是否"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " a gladiator* would live or die. A thumbs-up meant death; a thumbs-down meant life."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "h3",
        "type": "heading",
        "level": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "High five",
            "zh": "击掌"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Two LA Dodger* "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "teammates",
            "ref": "v-teammate"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " invented the “high five”. On October 2, 1977, after Dusty Baker had "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "hit",
            "ref": "v-hit"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " a "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "home run",
            "zh": "全垒打"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", Glenn Burke met him with his hand up over his head. Baker "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "reached up",
            "zh": "伸手"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " and hit Burke’s hand!"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "n1",
        "type": "note",
        "title": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Did you know?"
          }
        ],
        "content": [
          [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "*温斯顿·丘吉尔（Winston Churchill），英国政治家、历史学家和作家，两度担任英国首相，第二次世界大战中杰出的政治领袖之一。"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "*角斗士（gladiator），古罗马时期手持短剑、盾牌或其他武器彼此角斗，以博得观众喝彩的专业格斗士。"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "*洛杉矶道奇队（LA Dodger），加利福尼亚州洛杉矶的一支美国职业棒球大联盟球队，成立于1883年。"
            }
          ]
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
